# Kecktech Development Rules

You are assisting Jon (GitHub: Bizzo1975) with Kecktech platform services and custom application development. All work follows the Bizzo Development Workflow Framework (10-stage lifecycle, 5-project max).

## Tech Stack (Non-Negotiable)
- TypeScript strict mode — no `any` without explicit justification
- Next.js 14+ with App Router
- PostgreSQL + Prisma ORM (no raw SQL except migrations)
- NextAuth.js for auth (OAuth, credentials, SSO-ready)
- Tailwind CSS (client-themeable via CSS variables)
- Docker Compose for deployment
- Self-hosted on Proxmox — never default to cloud SaaS

## Code Standards
- UUIDs for primary keys
- `createdAt`/`updatedAt` on all tables
- Soft deletes (`deletedAt`) for user-facing data
- Error boundaries and graceful error handling
- Loading states for all async operations
- Mobile-first responsive design (320px-1920px)
- API-first: all business logic via typed API routes
- No hardcoded credentials — environment variables only

## File Conventions
- Components: PascalCase (`ContactCard.tsx`)
- Utilities: camelCase (`formatCurrency.ts`)
- API routes: kebab-case directories (`/api/purchase-orders/`)
- Prisma models: PascalCase singular (`model Invoice {}`)

## When Writing Code
1. Start with the Prisma schema if touching data models
2. Build API routes with input validation (zod preferred)
3. Create reusable components — check if similar exists first
4. Include proper TypeScript types for all props and returns
5. Add JSDoc comments on exported functions
6. Handle loading, error, and empty states in all UI

## Project Context Files
- `prompts/PROJECT-CONTEXT.md` — Master context (read first)
- `prompts/platform-services/` — BookStack, PeerTube, Rocket.Chat prompts
- `prompts/custom-apps/01-10` — Individual app specifications with data models

## Security Checklist (Every Feature)
- [ ] Input validation on all user inputs
- [ ] RBAC check on protected routes
- [ ] CSRF protection on mutations
- [ ] Rate limiting on public endpoints
- [ ] No secrets in code or logs
- [ ] SQL injection prevention (Prisma handles this)
- [ ] XSS prevention (React handles most, sanitize rich text)
